1
00:00:00,333 --> 00:00:03,503
Two thousand two hundred years in the ground.

2
00:00:03,503 --> 00:00:09,211
And this bronze sword came out still sharp, still bright, barely touched by rust.

3
00:00:09,211 --> 00:00:15,199
For decades, people said the reason was a secret chemical coating, a lost technology.

4
00:00:15,666 --> 00:00:24,433
The story went that Qin craftsmen coated their weapons in chromium, a method the modern world only patented in the twentieth century.

5
00:00:24,433 --> 00:00:27,333
Proof of something nobody should have known.

6
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:28,985
Alien engineers?

7
00:00:28,985 --> 00:00:31,207
A vanished super-civilisation?

8
00:00:31,207 --> 00:00:35,799
Or just a very good story that nobody checked for forty years?

9
00:00:36,266 --> 00:00:40,045
Tonight we run the case like a conservation lab.

10
00:00:40,045 --> 00:00:41,147
Sample intake.

11
00:00:41,147 --> 00:00:42,013
Microscope.

12
00:00:42,013 --> 00:00:43,430
Chemical analysis.

13
00:00:43,430 --> 00:00:44,218
Soil test.

14
00:00:44,218 --> 00:00:48,233
And a final report, where every claim gets a score.

15
00:00:48,700 --> 00:00:50,867
Facts first, theories labelled.

16
00:00:50,867 --> 00:00:52,266
Open the sample bag.

17
00:00:56,733 --> 00:00:57,642
Chapter one.

18
00:00:57,642 --> 00:00:58,703
Sample intake.

19
00:00:58,703 --> 00:01:03,326
The date is the twenty-ninth of March, nineteen seventy-four.

20
00:01:03,326 --> 00:01:07,266
Farmland near Lintong, outside Xi'an, in a dry year.

21
00:01:07,733 --> 00:01:09,505
Farmers are digging a well.

22
00:01:09,505 --> 00:01:14,755
One of them, Yang Zhifa, with his brothers and a neighbour, hits something hard.

23
00:01:14,755 --> 00:01:15,346
Not rock.

24
00:01:15,346 --> 00:01:18,299
Fired clay, and then a clay head, staring up.

25
00:01:18,766 --> 00:01:27,366
They had found the army of the first emperor of China, Qin Shi Huang, buried near his tomb in the late third century BCE.

26
00:01:27,833 --> 00:01:32,933
The largest pit is about two hundred thirty metres long and sixty-two wide.

27
00:01:32,933 --> 00:01:39,666
More than three thousand figures stand in it, and the four main pits lie roughly seven metres down.

28
00:01:40,133 --> 00:01:46,082
Every face is different, though they were built from moulds, with details added by hand.

29
00:01:46,082 --> 00:01:49,799
An industrial army, made like a modern production line.

30
00:01:50,266 --> 00:01:51,347
And the weapons.

31
00:01:51,347 --> 00:02:00,133
More than forty thousand bronze items have been recovered: swords, spears, halberds, crossbow triggers, and arrowheads in bundles.

32
00:02:00,599 --> 00:02:03,655
Most weapons were looted or rotted long ago.

33
00:02:03,655 --> 00:02:07,266
The ones that survived are the samples on our bench.

34
00:02:07,733 --> 00:02:10,462
One sword in particular became famous.

35
00:02:10,462 --> 00:02:14,699
Bright, sharp, and in a condition that made people ask how.

36
00:02:15,166 --> 00:02:16,243
Intake complete.

37
00:02:16,243 --> 00:02:21,900
Question for the lab: why did these weapons survive when others turn to green crust?

38
00:02:22,366 --> 00:02:23,140
Chapter two.

39
00:02:23,140 --> 00:02:23,785
The claim.

40
00:02:23,785 --> 00:02:26,300
Where did the chromium story come from?

41
00:02:26,766 --> 00:02:31,137
Analysis of some of the swords found chromium on the surface.

42
00:02:31,137 --> 00:02:35,866
A thin layer, a few micrometres thick, was reported on the blades.

43
00:02:36,333 --> 00:02:38,313
Chromium resists corrosion.

44
00:02:38,313 --> 00:02:42,493
That is why modern steel and car parts are chrome plated.

45
00:02:42,493 --> 00:02:45,499
So the idea seemed to explain everything.

46
00:02:45,966 --> 00:02:54,316
Popular versions added that the Qin had used chromate treatment, a process people link to the nineteen thirties in Germany.

47
00:02:54,316 --> 00:02:58,933
I could not verify that patent claim, so we mark it as popular lore.

48
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:00,604
And then the leap.

49
00:03:00,604 --> 00:03:04,285
If ancient China had chromate coating, who taught them?

50
00:03:04,285 --> 00:03:08,033
Cue the lost civilisation and the visitors from the sky.

51
00:03:08,500 --> 00:03:11,861
The claim spread because it is so easy to believe.

52
00:03:11,861 --> 00:03:16,566
A museum case, a shining blade, a number with the word chromium in it.

53
00:03:17,033 --> 00:03:19,889
But a coating is a claim about intention.

54
00:03:19,889 --> 00:03:23,233
It says someone applied the chromium on purpose.

55
00:03:23,233 --> 00:03:24,766
Science can test that.

56
00:03:25,233 --> 00:03:29,093
So in this lab, we do not ask whether chromium is there.

57
00:03:29,093 --> 00:03:31,300
We ask where, how much, and why.

58
00:03:31,766 --> 00:03:33,195
Question one logged.

59
00:03:33,195 --> 00:03:35,266
Next station: the microscope.

60
00:03:35,733 --> 00:03:36,725
Chapter three.

61
00:03:36,725 --> 00:03:37,789
The microscope.

62
00:03:37,789 --> 00:03:46,933
Researchers from University College London and the Emperor Qin Shihuang's Mausoleum Site Museum looked at the weapons themselves.

63
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:49,609
They studied hundreds of pieces.

64
00:03:49,609 --> 00:03:57,066
In total, four hundred sixty-four weapon parts were analysed, a very large sample for this kind of question.

65
00:03:57,533 --> 00:04:02,936
Under magnification, the surface of the metal is not the mirror we imagine.

66
00:04:02,936 --> 00:04:04,161
Corrosion exists.

67
00:04:04,161 --> 00:04:06,466
Some of it is thin, some patchy.

68
00:04:06,933 --> 00:04:08,218
And here is a clue.

69
00:04:08,218 --> 00:04:16,000
Many of these weapons had wooden or bamboo shafts, and the shafts were covered with lacquer, a black resin coating.

70
00:04:16,466 --> 00:04:19,595
Lacquer was a high-status material in Qin China.

71
00:04:19,595 --> 00:04:23,766
And it was part of the weapon wherever the blade met the handle.

72
00:04:24,233 --> 00:04:26,239
So the team did something simple.

73
00:04:26,239 --> 00:04:30,433
They mapped where the chromium appeared on each weapon, part by part.

74
00:04:30,899 --> 00:04:32,470
The pattern is not random.

75
00:04:32,470 --> 00:04:36,699
Chromium was strongest where the metal had touched the lacquered wood.

76
00:04:37,166 --> 00:04:40,160
A coating you apply on purpose goes everywhere.

77
00:04:40,160 --> 00:04:44,300
A smear you pick up from lacquer goes only where the lacquer was.

78
00:04:44,766 --> 00:04:45,628
Chapter four.

79
00:04:45,628 --> 00:04:46,755
The spectrometer.

80
00:04:46,755 --> 00:04:50,933
A machine that reads the elements on a surface, point by point.

81
00:04:51,399 --> 00:04:57,803
The result, in the numbers: chromium was found on fewer than ten percent of the weapons tested.

82
00:04:57,803 --> 00:05:00,566
Thirty-seven weapons, not the whole army.

83
00:05:01,033 --> 00:05:07,432
If the Qin had chromium plated their weapons as a standard process, almost all should have shown it.

84
00:05:07,432 --> 00:05:08,199
They do not.

85
00:05:08,666 --> 00:05:14,404
The chromium also followed the type of artefact, not the state of preservation.

86
00:05:14,404 --> 00:05:17,673
Well-preserved swords without chromium exist.

87
00:05:17,673 --> 00:05:20,433
Corroded ones with chromium exist too.

88
00:05:20,899 --> 00:05:25,295
If the chromium were the shield, the protected pieces would carry it.

89
00:05:25,295 --> 00:05:26,059
They do not.

90
00:05:26,059 --> 00:05:27,333
The link is missing.

91
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:30,384
Then the team measured the lacquer itself.

92
00:05:30,384 --> 00:05:32,600
And the lacquer is rich in chromium.

93
00:05:33,066 --> 00:05:45,199
A later study found Qin lacquer contains about zero point zero seven six micrograms of chromium per milligram, and the soil around about zero point zero six six.

94
00:05:45,666 --> 00:05:52,000
The lab's own conclusion in plain words: the lacquer is the unintended source of the chromium.

95
00:05:52,466 --> 00:05:53,366
Chapter five.

96
00:05:53,366 --> 00:05:54,473
The replication.

97
00:05:54,473 --> 00:05:58,833
If chromate coating really protected bronze, you can test that.

98
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:06,866
The team made bronze test pieces with modern chromate conversion coatings, and left others plain, as controls.

99
00:06:07,333 --> 00:06:13,533
Then they buried them in soils and aged them in accelerated conditions, to see which survive.

100
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,014
The coating was not the star.

101
00:06:16,014 --> 00:06:16,917
The soil was.

102
00:06:16,917 --> 00:06:20,600
In the acidic soil, even the treated pieces corroded.

103
00:06:21,066 --> 00:06:26,554
A piece left in low-pH, low-quality soil corroded no matter what it wore.

104
00:06:26,554 --> 00:06:28,433
Chemistry beats ornament.

105
00:06:28,899 --> 00:06:36,699
Meanwhile, alkaline fine-grained soil kept bronze in surprisingly good shape, even without a magic coating.

106
00:06:37,166 --> 00:06:41,364
And the claimed coating was ten to fifteen micrometres thick.

107
00:06:41,364 --> 00:06:46,800
That is thinner than a human hair, far thinner than anyone could verify by eye.

108
00:06:47,266 --> 00:06:52,100
The replication did not support an ancient chrome coating as the preservative.

109
00:06:52,566 --> 00:06:53,419
Chapter six.

110
00:06:53,419 --> 00:06:54,413
The soil test.

111
00:06:54,413 --> 00:06:56,899
So why did so many weapons survive?

112
00:06:57,366 --> 00:07:01,694
The Qin pits were filled with very fine soil, packed tightly.

113
00:07:01,694 --> 00:07:05,100
Fine particles keep air and water moving slowly.

114
00:07:05,566 --> 00:07:08,461
The soil was also moderately alkaline.

115
00:07:08,461 --> 00:07:13,033
Alkaline conditions slow the corrosion of copper-tin bronze.

116
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:23,366
The bronze itself was a high-quality copper and tin alloy, with traces of nickel, magnesium and cobalt, and it was cast with real control.

117
00:07:23,833 --> 00:07:31,166
The pits were built as sealed halls: wooden roofs, mats and packed earth, made to protect the army in the afterlife.

118
00:07:31,633 --> 00:07:36,196
The same roofs later burned and fell, as armies and looters came.

119
00:07:36,196 --> 00:07:40,899
Fire, collapse and decay are why many figures were found in pieces.

120
00:07:41,366 --> 00:07:46,811
What survived intact did so by geography, luck and clean soil chemistry.

121
00:07:46,811 --> 00:07:48,399
No visitors required.

122
00:07:48,866 --> 00:07:50,133
Soil test complete.

123
00:07:50,133 --> 00:07:52,666
The environment preserved the weapons.

124
00:07:53,133 --> 00:07:54,070
Chapter seven.

125
00:07:54,070 --> 00:07:54,740
The craft.

126
00:07:54,740 --> 00:07:57,754
If there is no secret chemical, what is left?

127
00:07:57,754 --> 00:08:00,433
Something more impressive: organisation.

128
00:08:00,899 --> 00:08:04,017
Arrowheads were made in standardised batches.

129
00:08:04,017 --> 00:08:10,600
The chemistry of bundles of about a hundred points matches closely, a sign of batch production.

130
00:08:11,066 --> 00:08:13,373
The paint tells the same story.

131
00:08:13,373 --> 00:08:20,666
Cinnabar red, malachite green, azurite blue, and Han purple, a synthetic pigment, were all in use.

132
00:08:21,133 --> 00:08:25,793
Han purple is barium copper silicate, a manufactured pigment.

133
00:08:25,793 --> 00:08:26,938
Real chemistry.

134
00:08:26,938 --> 00:08:28,466
Not alien chemistry.

135
00:08:28,933 --> 00:08:38,415
And when the paint was first exposed to Xi'an's dry air, the lacquer underneath curled in about fifteen seconds and flaked within minutes.

136
00:08:38,415 --> 00:08:40,133
Fragile, brilliant, gone.

137
00:08:40,600 --> 00:08:47,466
The real wonder is a state that could mould, fire, paint and arm thousands of soldiers to a standard.

138
00:08:47,933 --> 00:08:48,683
Lab report.

139
00:08:48,683 --> 00:08:50,933
Time to score the chromium claim.

140
00:08:51,399 --> 00:08:54,269
Chromium exists on some weapons: evidence.

141
00:08:54,269 --> 00:08:57,139
A deliberate protective coating: debunked.

142
00:08:57,139 --> 00:09:02,333
Chromium on over ninety percent of weapons: false, under ten percent had it.

143
00:09:02,799 --> 00:09:06,581
Lacquer as the chromium source: strong evidence.

144
00:09:06,581 --> 00:09:10,127
Soil chemistry as the preservative: evidence.

145
00:09:10,127 --> 00:09:14,066
Lost technology or alien help: no evidence at all.

146
00:09:14,533 --> 00:09:15,348
The verdict.

147
00:09:15,348 --> 00:09:18,747
The chromium was real, but the coating was a myth.

148
00:09:18,747 --> 00:09:23,233
It was contamination from lacquer, and the real hero was the soil.

149
00:09:23,700 --> 00:09:31,993
The correction came from a joint team including the museum itself, published in Scientific Reports in twenty nineteen.

150
00:09:31,993 --> 00:09:35,366
Science corrected a forty-year belief in public.

151
00:09:35,833 --> 00:09:44,274
Next case: sixty-two schoolchildren in Zimbabwe in nineteen ninety-four, and what they said came down onto their playground.

152
00:09:44,274 --> 00:09:48,766
The story is very different, and the evidence is not a lab report.

153
00:09:49,233 --> 00:09:51,320
Did you believe the chrome story?

154
00:09:51,320 --> 00:09:56,633
Tell us in the comments, and subscribe for the next ancient mystery put to the test.
